spec:
  grid: 7-18 square (H=W) [observed]
  colors: 3 total — bg (dominant), divider_color, sprite_color
  divider:
    full-width solid horizontal row of divider_color
    position: rows above >= 3, rows below >= 3
  sprites:
    count: 1-5 4-connected monochromatic components of sprite_color, all above divider
    no two sprites share any column
    gap_to_divider: >=1 empty row between each sprite bottom and divider
    below_divider: entirely bg in input
    single_col: 0-2 sprites occupying one column; height 1-7
    multi_col: 0-3 sprites; each is a vertical spine (width-1 rows) plus one contiguous horizontal bar (width 2-3) — exactly one row is widest, strictly unique; bar contains the spine column; bbox height 1-5
  rule:
    clear original sprite pixels
    single_col sprites fall to grid bottom and delete divider pixel at their column (bg hole)
    multi_col sprites shift down so their unique widest row lands at divider_row-1; pixels crossing divider overwrite it (sprite_color replaces divider_color)
    moved sprites must not overlap each other or go out of bounds

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick H=W in 7-18, bg, divider_color, sprite_color (all distinct).
    2. Place divider row so above>=3 and below>=3.
    3. Decide sprite counts — n_single in 0-2, n_multi in 0-3, total>=1.
    4. Build multi-col sprites in their LANDED positions (widest row at divider_row-1, tail possibly crossing divider). Ensure no column overlap and sprites fit in grid. Record which divider pixels they overwrite.
    5. Build single-col sprites in their LANDED positions (bottom at row H-1). Ensure their column is not used by any multi-col sprite. Mark divider pixel at that column as bg hole.
    6. Derive INPUT by moving each sprite back up — multi-col sprites shift up by (divider_row-1-original_widest_row), single-col sprites shift up so they sit above divider with >=1 gap. Restore divider to full solid row.
    7. Verify all sprites are above divider in input with >=1 gap, and below-divider region is all bg.

